# Selected TODOs

Primary UI: the **Project TODO** canvas
[`todo.canvas.tsx`](C:/Users/kirpa/.cursor/projects/d-Projects-scrap-download/canvases/todo.canvas.tsx).

Selections persist in the sidecar next to that file:

`C:\Users\kirpa\.cursor\projects\d-Projects-scrap-download\canvases\todo.canvas.data.json`

## How to read selection

When the user asks to work on todos, selected items, or this list:

1. Read `todo.canvas.data.json` if it exists.
2. Find the `itemFlags` object (top-level or nested under a `state`/`keys` bag — use whichever shape the sidecar actually has).
3. **Selected** = any id whose flags have `work: true` and not `done: true`.
4. Match those ids to item text in the canvas seed `ITEMS` array, plus any `addedItems` in the sidecar (skip `removedIds`). Fall back to `TODO.md` for wording.
5. Implement **only** the selected items.

If the sidecar is missing or has no `work: true` entries, fall back to `TODO.md`:

- Selected = first box `[x]`/`[X]`, second still `[ ]`
- Done = second box `[x]`/`[X]`

Ignore unselected and already-done items.

## After finishing an item

1. In `todo.canvas.data.json`, set that id’s flags to `{ "work": false, "done": true }` (create the file / `itemFlags` object if needed, preserving other keys).
2. Update the matching line in `TODO.md`: Work `[ ]`, Done `[x]`, wrap text (and continuation lines) in `~~…~~`.

Do not start other backlog items unless the user selects them.
